{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015369-forge-purpose-magical-items-and-unawakened","id":1015369,"title":"Forge Purpose, Magical items and unAwakened","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-10T14:20:45-08:00","id":1015369,"title":"Forge Purpose, Magical items and unAwakened","content":"So, I thought about designing an object that allows Sleepers and Sleepwalkers to gain the benefits of this spell without the mage forcing specific Obsessions on them. However, I am not sure what the somewhat nebulous rules allow. As of now I can think of two options, prefering the first one:<br /> <br /> 1. An Enhanced Item replicates the Forge Purpose spell with one Reach built into this persistent spell, which defines the Obsession as &quot;being equivalent to the Aspiration of the wearer that could behavior-wise be extreme enough to be defined as obsession, just not the magical kind of Obsession.&quot; This would allow the Sleeper/Sleepwalker to gain Arcane Beats for their obsessive behavior. The problem here is that I don't know if this kind of definition is allowed (Practice of Dynamics would be powerful enough to change the entire definition of the Obsession on a whim, for example, so I don't think my definition steps into this area, it's always the same definition).<br /> <br /> 2. Or it could be an Imbued Item with the same spell, the activation trigger being a situation, where if the person's Aspiration were to be an Obsession, they would earn an Arcane Beat at that moment. At that point the item activates, using a point of Mana and temporarily gives the individual the Obsession. Here I'm not sure what the actual Obsession could be, because the Sleeper/Sleepwalker casts the spell, not any mage, and so there isn't an Obsession to be given by anybody (here if the person's non-magical obsession was possible to use as a template, it would be enough).<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, so what do you think? Are any of the two options above viable, or did I overlook something obvious?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T15:22:57-08:00","id":1015380,"title":"","content":"The Obsession is chosen at the time that the Imbued Item is triggered. I have no idea why you're talking about the Dynamics and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T15:45:55-08:00","id":1015388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015369-forge-purpose-magical-items-and-unawakened?p=1015380#post1015380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Obsession is chosen at the time that the Imbued Item is triggered. I have no idea why you're talking about the Dynamics and stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, thanks. I guess the spell description mentioning the mage deciding the Obsession, and not a caster in general, was because an imbued item with this spell is somewhat of a niche idea.<br /> <br /> As for mentioning Dynamics in the first option, I just considered the changing nature of the Obsession. Sleeper #1 gets the item and gains beats through different actions than Sleeper #2 later on using the same item, because they have different Aspirations they obsess about. The definition of the Obsession in this case was somewhat abstract to at least consider Dynamics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T16:15:19-08:00","id":1015400,"title":"","content":"The person using the item would be considered the caster. The exception would most likely be if the Mage who imbued the item hadn't relinquished it in which case he can change its factors or cancel it anytime that it's used.<br /> <br /> Anyway, once the Obsession is set on a target it doesn't change. It's also two different instances of the spell so nothing is changing on that end either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}